#!/usr/bin/python3
"""KantanOS Watch TV: live TV like a cable box, for the remote, keyboard or mouse.

  Up / Down, Page Up / Down, CH+ / CH-   next / previous channel (in the list you picked it from)
  0-9                                     type a channel number
  OK / Enter                              what's on (press again for the guide)
  Right, G, Guide, Menu                   the guide: countries, topics, what's on when
  Left, Back-and-forth                    the channel you watched before
  R, Record                               record what's on (or the programme chosen in the guide)
  F                                       favourite channel
  /, S, Search                            find a channel or show: "star trek*", "*news*" (* = anything, ? = one letter)
  Esc / Back                              close; press twice to leave
  Mouse: click for what's on, right-click for the guide, wheel to change channel, double-click for full screen.
  In the guide: click the country (left or right half) for the other countries you chose; the
  wheel over the left side scrolls the categories; Recordings and Settings are at the bottom.

Channels and sorting: /usr/share/kantanos/tv/lineup.py. Guide: guide.py. Recordings: recorder.py
and the kantanos-tv-recorder user service.
"""
